> [!answer]
> A Theory X head assumes teachers **dislike work and avoid responsibility**, so he or she will:
> - **supervise closely** and check attendance, lesson notes and punctuality;
> - **rely on threats, queries and punishment**;
> - **centralise decisions** and rarely delegate or consult;
> - communicate **top-down** through orders and memos;
> - show **little trust** or recognition, lowering staff morale.

> [!answer]
> A Theory Y head assumes teachers **like work, are self-directed and seek responsibility**, so he or she will:
> - **delegate** responsibilities and **involve staff in decisions**;
> - use **minimal close supervision**, trusting teachers;
> - **motivate** through recognition, growth and job enrichment;
> - encourage **initiative and creativity**;
> - keep **two-way communication** open.
